      "text": "Adam and Eve our first parents, 1 Ne. 5:11. driven from garden, 2 Ne. 2:19. if Adam had not transgressed, he would not have fallen, 2 Ne. 2:22. Adam fell that men might be, 2 Ne. 2:25. the Holy One suffered pains of all who belong to family of Adam, 2 Ne. 9:21. Christ’s blood atones for all who have fallen by transgression of Adam, Mosiah 3:11. as in Adam, or by nature, men fall, Mosiah 3:16. natural man an enemy to God since Fall of Adam, Mosiah 3:19. justice could not deny Adam should fall because of partaking of forbidden fruit, Mosiah 3:26.",
